        "id": 1287197
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-10-01T15:28:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It seems like the intent was to be able to compile without this config, based on the \"IS_ENABLED\" usage below.  What kind of build errors do you see without Try.SRC enabled?\n\nAlso, if we go the route of making Try.SRC optional and adding ifdefs, that would potentially free up devices from needing a couple of states (Try.SRC and TryWait.SNK).  Not a big flash win, but something.",
      "revId": "e0c44bc455defbc2ebf8f36f24b1a811443e6103",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b948e884_8ea66a7f",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_tc_drp_acc_trysrc_sm.c",
        "patchSetId": 32
      },
      "lineNbr": 472,
