        "id": 1123814
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-10-01T16:19:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, the IS_ENABLED is used in various places, but there are still issues.\n\n/* Generate a compiler error if invalid states are referenced */\n#ifndef CONFIG_USB_PD_TRY_SRC\n#define TC_TRY_SRC\tTC_TRY_SRC_UNDEFINED\n#define TC_TRY_WAIT_SNK\tTC_TRY_WAIT_SNK_UNDEFINED\n#endif\n\nBecause the try.src states only exist if the config option is defined, then these statements cause issues.\n\nset_state_tc(port, tryWait ? TC_TRY_WAIT_SNK : TC_UNATTACHED_SNK);\n\nTC_TRY_WAIT_SNK is defined as TC_TRY_WAIT_SNK_UNDEFINED\n\nIn this particular function, I believe the issues that variables like pd_try_src_override don\u0027t exist so you get compiler errors.",
      "parentUuid": "24f63fad_9fe79b3e",
      "revId": "e0c44bc455defbc2ebf8f36f24b1a811443e6103",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
